Q: Managing ORDS with mend renovate A: <p>Maybe something like this would work since that website only has major.minor syntax</p>
<pre><code>{
  &quot;customManagers&quot;: [
    {
      &quot;customType&quot;: &quot;regex&quot;,
      &quot;fileMatch&quot;: [&quot;(^|/)Dockerfile$&quot;],
      &quot;matchStrings&quot;: [
        &quot;datasource=(?&lt;datasource&gt;.*?) depName=(?&lt;depName&gt;.*?)\\sARG ORDS_VERSION=(?&lt;currentValue&gt;.*)\\s&quot;
      ],
      &quot;registryUrlTemplate&quot;: &quot;https://docs.oracle.com/en/database/oracle/oracle-rest-data-services/&quot;,
      &quot;versioningTemplate&quot;: &quot;regex:^(?&lt;major&gt;\\d+)\\.(?&lt;minor&gt;\\d+)$&quot;
    }
  ],
  &quot;packageRules&quot;: [
    {
      &quot;matchPackageNames&quot;: [&quot;oracle-ords&quot;],
      &quot;extractVersion&quot;: &quot;Oracle REST Data Services (?&lt;version&gt;\\d+\\.\\d+)&quot;
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre>

Q: Java Record with @Builder.Default A: <p>You can rely on a <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/javase/specs/jls/se21/html/jls-8.html#jls-8.10.4.2" rel="nofollow noreferrer">compact constructor</a> for setting the defaults:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@Builder
public record FileProperties(String directory, String name, String extension) {

    public FileProperties {
        // no need to rewrite all fields, just the ones that need a default, eg:
        extension = Objects.requireNonNullElse(extension, &quot;.txt&quot;);
    }

}
</code></pre>
